# Reference copy of Boron Panel's API-only secrets file. Real deployments
# install this at /etc/boron/api-secrets.env, mode 0640, owned
# root:boron-api -- the unprivileged boron-api process needs to read this
# one (unlike secrets.env, which stays root:root/0600 and boron-api can't
# read at all). NEVER commit the real file to git. See README.md
# "Configuration files" for the exact setup command
# (SESSION_SECRET=$(openssl rand -hex 32)).

# Signs the session cookie (itsdangerous). If this isn't set, the panel
# runs with an insecure, obviously-fake default and refuses to treat any
# session as authenticated for real use (shared/config.py
# require_secure_session_secret) -- generate a real one before going live.
SESSION_SECRET=REPLACE_WITH_OPENSSL_RAND_HEX_32
